//! The raster package: triangles turned into the surface a camera sees,
//! as Kernels. It is the rasterizer's law written where every backend runs
//! it alike — the same pixel centres, the same edges, the same nearest
//! fragment — so a surface is the same on the interpreter, the JIT and
//! the GPU, and anything about it can be changed without Rust.
package raster@1 { language = 2; ir = 1; }

use "kernels/";
